ersection:\n\n$$\n[\\frac{1+2{e}^{6}}{{e}^{6}},\\infty )\\cap (2,\\infty )=[\\frac{1+2{e}^{6}}{{e}^{6}},\\infty )\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\in [\\frac{1+2{e}^{6}}{{e}^{6}},\\infty ),$ which can also be written as $x\\ge \\frac{1+2{e}^{6}}{{e}^{6}}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428788 #edb/ref 1030 1.0 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428788 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 2 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1, 2]; waits [1, 1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (2/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 2858->1643. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428788 #edb/ref 1036 #edb/ref 17592186049670 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428789 #edb/ref 1030 0.25 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428789 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 4 eligible passed source activities = 0.250000; nearest selected fraction = 1/4. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/4 (1/4). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not 